## The problem

Most nutrition content either sells something or says "it depends". Neither tells you how strong the evidence actually is.

## What I built

An index of 14 categories — macros, supplements and vitamins. Every claim gets a grade from A to D, a plain-language reason and numbered sources, with study type and industry ties marked on each one. Each category has its own 3D particle form.

## How it runs

One research agent per category writes a structured JSON file. Every uncertain citation gets checked against PubMed, a script builds the site, and I assign the final grades.
